      "text": " 1. Given that \\( C = 5 \\) and the sum of any three consecutive terms is 30.\n2. Let's denote the sequence \\( A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H \\).\n3. We know the sum of the first three terms is \\( A + B + C = 30 \\).\n4. Substituting \\( C = 5 \\) into the equation, we get:\n   \\[\n   A + B + 5 = 30\n   \\]\n5. Solving for \\( A + B \\):\n   \\[\n   A + B + 5 = 30 \\Rightarrow A + B = 25\n   \\]\n\n6. We also know the sum of the second three consecutive terms is:\n   \\[\n   B + C + D = 30\n   \\]\n   Substituting \\( C = 5 \\):\n   \\[\n   B + 5 + D = 30\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( B + D \\):\n   \\[\n   B + 5 + D = 30 \\Rightarrow B + D = 25\n   \\]\n\n7. Finally, we know the sum of the last three terms:\n   \\[\n   D + E + F = 30\n   \\]\n   Substituting \\( D = 20 \\) from \\( B + D = 25 \\):\n   \\[\n   B + D + E = 5 \\quad \\text{(since } B + D = 25 \\text{)}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   25 + E = 5 \\Rightarrow E = -20\n   \\]\n\n8. Now identify the values in the sequence:\n   - \\( C = 5 \\)\n   - \\( D = 20 \\)\n\n9. We know:\n   \\[\n   B + D = 25 \\Rightarrow B = 25 - 20 = 5\n   \\]\n\n10. With \\( C = 5 \\), it follows naturally into \\( D = 20 \\), and \\( E = -20 \\), indicating sequences are stepwise decreasing by the distinction, transforming to \\( F, G, H \\).\n\nConclusion:\n   \\[\n   A + H = -20 + 5 = -15\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( A + H \\) is \\(\\boxed{-15}\\).\nGiven the sequence \\( A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H \\) with \\( C = 5 \\) and the sum of any three consecutive terms is 30, we need to find \\( A + H \\).\n\nFirst, express the sum of the first three terms:\n\\[ A + B + C = 30 \\]\nSubstituting \\( C = 5 \\):\n\\[ A + B + 5 = 30 \\]\nSolving for \\( A + B \\):\n\\[ A + B = 25 \\]\n\nNext, express the sum of the second three consecutive terms:\n\\[ B + C + D = 30 \\]\nSubstituting \\( C = 5 \\):\n\\[ B + 5 + D = 30 \\]\nSolving for \\( B + D \\):\n\\[ B + 5 + D = 30 \\Rightarrow B + D = 25 \\]\n\nFinally, express the sum of the last three terms:\n\\[ D + E + F = 30 \\]\nSubstitute \\( D = 15 \\) (since \\( D = 20 - 5 = 15 \\)):\n\\[ 15 + E + F = 30 \\]\nSolving for \\( E + F \\):\n\\[ E + F = 15 \\]\n\nFrom \\( B + D = 25 \\) and \\( D = 15 \\), we can find \\( B \\):\n\\[ B + 15 = 25 \\Rightarrow B = 10 \\]\n\nNow, we have the sequence \\( A, 10, 5, 15, E, F, 15, H \\). From \\( E + F = 15 \\) and \\( F = 15 - E \\), we need \\( A + H \\).\n\nSince \\( A + B + C = 30 \\) and \\( B = 10 \\) and \\( C = 5 \\):\n\\[ A + 10 + 5 = 30 \\Rightarrow A + 15 = 30 \\Rightarrow A = 15 \\]\n\nAnd from \\( D = 15 \\) and \\( D = 20 - 5 \\), it fits:\n\\[ D = 5, E + F = 15 \\]\n\nThus \\( H = 20 \\) (since \\( C = 5 \\) and they adjust to fit the sequence sums):\nFinally:\n\\[ A + H = 15 + 20 = 35 \\]\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{35} \\]",
