    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Given the sequence \\(A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H\\) with \\(C = 5\\) and the property that the sum of any three consecutive terms is 30, we can set up the equations accordingly. Let's denote the sum of any three consecutive terms as follows:\n\n\\[A + B + C = 30\\]\n\\[B + C + D = 30\\]\n\\[C + D + E = 30\\]\n\\[D + E + F = 30\\]\n\\[E + F + G = 30\\]\n\\[F + G + H = 30\\]\n\nWe know \\(C = 5\\). Substituting this value into the equations, we get:\n\n\\[A + B + 5 = 30\\]\n\\[B + 5 + D = 30\\]\n\\[5 + D + E = 30\\]\n\\[D + E + F = 30\\]\n\\[E + F + G = 30\\]\n\\[F + G + H = 30\\]\n\nFrom the first equation, we can solve for \\(A + B\\):\n\n\\[A + B = 30 - 5 = 25\\]\n\nFrom the second equation, solve for \\(D + B\\):\n\n\\[B + 5 + D = 30 \\implies D + B = 25 - 5 = 20\\]\n\nFrom the third equation, we have:\n\n\\[5 + D + E = 30 \\implies D + E = 25\\]\n\nFrom the fourth equation, we have:\n\n\\[D + E + F = 30\\]\n\nSubtracting \\(D + E\\) from both sides of the equation \\(D + E + F = 30\\), we get:\n\n\\[F = 30 - 25 = 5\\]\n\nSince \\(F = 5\\) and \\(H = 30 - (F + G) = 30 - 5 - G\\), we substitute \\(F = 5\\) back to find \\(G\\):\n\n\\[5 + G = 30 - 5 \\implies G = 25\\]\n\nNow we know:\n\n\\[H = 30 - 5 = 25\\]\n\nSo, the values we have are:\n\n\\[A + B = 25\\]\n\\[D + E = 25\\]\n\\[H = 25\\]\n\\[A + H = 25\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(A + H\\) is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{40}\\]",
